[{"id":2720463175,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6iJvlH","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"The idea of this PR is welcome! Seems like a common enough pattern to support with some functional sugar.\r\nHowever, I prefer #100603's formulation over this one:\r\n\r\n```c++\r\n// Original\r\nSpatial * my_obj = Object::cast_to<Spatial>(ObjectDB::get_instance(object_id));\r\n// #100603\r\nSpatial * my_obj = ObjectDB::get_instance<Spatial>(object_id);\r\n// This PR\r\nSpatial * my_obj = object_id.get_object<Type>();\r\n```\r\n\r\nWhile your formulation is shorter, in #100603's version it's clearer that it uses the `ClassDB`, which I think is very important to understand the code at a glance.\r\n\r\nAs for the `Ref` version, I'm more neutral on this being added since I like `Ref` creation being explicit. But I'd be OK with `ObjectDB::get_ref<Spatial>(object_id)`.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/100602#pullrequestreview-2720463175","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine